      "tabTitle": "The 15° Rule",
      "title": "Earth's Rotation & Time",
      "description": "Understanding why time changes.",
      "initialRotation": [0, -10, 0],
      "zoomFactor": 1.2,
      "hideDefaultLines": false,
      
      "lines": [
        { "type": "lon", "value": 0, "color": "#ef4444", "label": "0°", "dashed": false },
        { "type": "lon", "value": 15, "color": "#facc15", "label": "15°", "dashed": true },
        { "type": "lon", "value": 30, "color": "#facc15", "label": "30°", "dashed": true },
        { "type": "lon", "value": 45, "color": "#facc15", "label": "45°", "dashed": true }
      ],

      "steps": [
        "The Earth rotates <b>360°</b> in <b>24 hours</b>.",
        "<b>Math:</b> 360 ÷ 24 = 15.",
        "<b>The Golden Rule:</b> Every <b>15°</b> of Longitude = <b>1 Hour</b> of time difference.",
        "<b>East</b> is always AHEAD (+). <b>West</b> is always BEHIND (-)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tabTitle": "GMT ➡ East",
      "title": "Case 1: Greenwich to East",
      "description": "It is 12:00 PM at Greenwich (0°). What time is it in Madagascar (45°E)?",
      "initialRotation": [-25, -10, 0],
      "zoomFactor": 1.4,
      "hideDefaultLines": true,

      "lines": [
        { "type": "lon", "value": 0, "color": "#3b82f6", "label": "GMT (0°)" },
        { "type": "lon", "value": 45, "color": "#facc15", "label": "45°E" }
      ],
      "connection": { "from": [0, 51], "to": [45, -18] },
      "markers": [
          { "label": "London (12:00 PM)", "lat": 51.5, "lon": 0, "color": "#3b82f6" },
          { "label": "Madagascar (?)", "lat": -18, "lon": 45, "color": "#ef4444" }
      ],

      "steps": [
        "<b>Step 1 (Difference):</b> 45° - 0° = <b>45°</b>.",
        "<b>Step 2 (Hours):</b> 45 ÷ 15 = <b>3 Hours</b>.",
        "<b>Step 3 (Decide):</b> East is <b>Ahead</b>. We ADD time.",
        "<b>Step 4 (Calc):</b> 12:00 + 3 hours = <b>3:00 PM</b>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tabTitle": "GMT ➡ West",
      "title": "Case 2: Greenwich to West",
      "description": "It is 4:00 PM at Greenwich (0°). What time is it in Brazil (45°W)?",
      "initialRotation": [20, -10, 0],
      "zoomFactor": 1.4,
      "hideDefaultLines": true,

      "lines": [
        { "type": "lon", "value": 0, "color": "#3b82f6", "label": "GMT (0°)" },
        { "type": "lon", "value": -45, "color": "#ef4444", "label": "45°W" }
      ],
      "connection": { "from": [0, 51], "to": [-45, -14] },
      "markers": [
          { "label": "London (4:00 PM)", "lat": 51.5, "lon": 0, "color": "#3b82f6" },
          { "label": "Brazil (?)", "lat": -14, "lon": -45, "color": "#ef4444" }
      ],

      "steps": [
        "<b>Step 1 (Difference):</b> 45° - 0° = <b>45°</b>.",
        "<b>Step 2 (Hours):</b> 45 ÷ 15 = <b>3 Hours</b>.",
        "<b>Step 3 (Decide):</b> West is <b>Behind</b>. We SUBTRACT time.",
        "<b>Step 4 (Calc):</b> 4:00 - 3 hours = <b>1:00 PM</b>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "tabTitle": "East ➡ West",
      "title": "Case 3: Crossing the Prime Meridian",
      "description": "It is 2:00 PM in Cairo (30°E). What time is it in Verde (30°W)?",
      "initialRotation": [0, 0, 0],
      "zoomFactor": 1.3,
      "hideDefaultLines": true,

      "lines": [
        { "type": "lon", "value": 30, "color": "#3b82f6", "label": "30°E" },
        { "type": "lon", "value": 0, "color": "#94a3b8", "dashed": true },
        { "type": "lon", "value": -30, "color": "#ef4444", "label": "30°W" }
      ],
      "connection": { "from": [30, 30], "to": [-30, 14] },
      "markers": [
          { "label": "Cairo (2:00 PM)", "lat": 30, "lon": 30, "color": "#3b82f6" },
          { "label": "Verde (?)", "lat": 14, "lon": -30, "color": "#ef4444" }
      ],

      "steps": [
        "<b>Step 1 (Degrees):</b> One is East, One is West. We <b>ADD degrees</b> first.",
        "30° + 30° = <b>60° Total Distance</b>.",
        "<b>Step 2 (Hours):</b> 60 ÷ 15 = <b>4 Hours</b> difference.",
        "<b>Step 3 (Decide):</b> Moving West means SUBTRACT.",
        "<b>Step 4:</b> 2:00 PM - 4 hours = <b>10:00 AM</b>."
      ]
    }
  ]
}